The .abi and .bin files here are frozen. They are the ERC20/721/1155 pointer contracts
deployed on chain before pointer creation was retired. The bytecode is embedded so that
`debug_trace*` can replay historical pointer creation, and the ABIs so that the
registry queries and the CosmWasm ERC helpers can call a pointer that is already
deployed.

Nothing regenerates these artifacts. Their Solidity sources are not in the tree:
a rebuild could only produce bytecode that differs from what is deployed, which would
break the replay these files exist for.
